         <t:abstract>
            <t:p><t:foreign xml:lang="gez">Dǝrsāna Gabrǝʾel</t:foreign> is a collection of 12 monthly readings in honour of <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4377Gabriel">Gabriel</t:persName>, beginning with the
               month of <t:foreign xml:lang="gez">Tāḫśāś</t:foreign> (cf. <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/KBEJNK4A"><seg type="encyclopediaArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Samuel2005EAEDersanaGabreel"/><title level="a">Dǝrsanä Gäbrǝʾel</title><title type="short">EAe</title><title level="m">Encyclopaedia Aethiopica</title><author><name>Samuel Yalew</name></author><editor><forename>Siegbert</forename><surname>Uhlig</surname></editor><pubPlace>Wiesbaden</pubPlace><publisher>Harrassowitz Verlag</publisher><date>2005</date><biblScope unit="volume">II</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">137b-138a</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Samuel2005EAEDersanaGabreel</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Samuel2005EAEDersanaGabreel</note></t:bibl>). Each section usually includes at least one homily, one miracle, one
               commemorative note concerning the apparition of the Archangel to a biblical or a saintly figure, and a <t:foreign xml:lang="gez">salām</t:foreign>-hymn to
               <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4377Gabriel">Gabriel</t:persName> or to other saints or another rhyming strophe in honour of Gabriel, and may also be preceded by a rhyming preamble.
               In some manuscripts, like <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/BAVet82">Vatican City, Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Aeth. 82</t:ref>, the <t:foreign xml:lang="gez">Dǝrsāna Gabrǝʾel</t:foreign> is divided into 7 readings, one for each
               weekday, and the miracles are grouped separately.
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
